\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 Job Title: Senior Java Microservices Server Engineer \
Job Summary: We are seeking a highly skilled and experienced Senior Java Microservices Server Engineer to join our dynamic team. The ideal candidate will have over 10 years of experience in backend development, specializing in Java, Spring Boot, and Spring MVC. This role requires strong problem-solving abilities and leadership experience, as you will be responsible for guiding a team of engineers in delivering high-quality microservices solutions. The position is available in both San Francisco, CA, and New Jersey. Key Responsibilities: - Design, develop, and maintain scalable microservices using Java, Spring Boot, and Spring MVC. - Lead and mentor a team of engineers, fostering a collaborative and innovative work environment. - Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features. - Troubleshoot and resolve production issues, ensuring high availability and performance of applications. - Implement best practices for software development, including code reviews, testing, and continuous integration. - Stay updated with emerging technologies and industry trends to drive innovation within the team. Required Qualifications and Skills: - Bachelor\'92s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field. - 10+ years of experience in Java backend development, with a strong focus on microservices architecture. - Proficiency in Spring Boot and Spring MVC frameworks. - Strong hands-on experience with problem-solving and debugging complex applications. - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively in a team environment. Preferred Experience: - Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud. - Familiarity with containerization technologies like Docker and orchestration tools like Kubernetes. - Knowledge of database technologies such as SQL and NoSQL. Work Environment: We pride ourselves on maintaining an inclusive and collaborative company culture that values diversity and innovation. Our team is dedicated to continuous learning and professional development, providing opportunities for growth and advancement. Certifications or Tools Required: - Relevant certifications in Java or cloud technologies are a plus. - Familiarity with Agile methodologies and tools such as JIRA or Confluence is preferred.}